CloudBurrow patch 106 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#2012). Applies after patch 0104.

BigQuery: "Each table, query result, or view definition can have up to
10,000 columns. This includes nested and repeated columns."
(https://docs.cloud.google.com/bigquery/quotas). The engine's SQLite
holds 32,767 columns (go-sqlite3-wasm patch 0105), and CloudBurrow's
front checked only tables.insert and tables.patch, so a query, CREATE
TABLE, CREATE TABLE ... AS SELECT or CREATE VIEW of more columns ran.

The analyzer now refuses each of them over 10,000 columns, a STRUCT's
fields (at every depth, and an ARRAY of STRUCT's) counted, before
anything runs or is made, with "Too many columns: the <query result |
table | view> has N columns, including nested and repeated columns; a
table, query result, or view definition can have up to 10000 columns".
BigQuery documents no message for it. The column of the time a row was
streamed the engine adds to a table (_PARTITION_STREAMED) is not
counted. Regression test TestTenThousandColumnLimit.

